      "content": "okay, i see. i'm just a bit worried because the HelioMove patent actually mentions a similar grade of polymer for the sensor housing and the way they handle the axis realignment seems pretty close to ours on paper. if the examiner catches that similarity early on, it might trigger an obviousness rejection and kill the whole application. are you absolutely sure the material and sensor differences are substantial enough to carry the novelty claim? i'd hate to find out later that we missed a core overlap.",
